        "stop_reason": {
          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "## Result\n\nA complete, general INI parser and printer in MoonBit for this repo's dialect. `moon check` reports **0 errors**; `moon test` reports **55/55 passing** (the 12 public cases incl. both quickcheck properties + 43 conformance tests I added).\n\n### What was built\n\n| file | lines | role |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [chars.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\chars.mbt) | 128 | blank/control char sets, clamped trimming/copy helpers, LF+CRLF line splitting |\n| [value.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\value.mbt) | 220 | the three value carriers, per-carrier escape decoding, quoted scanning, unquoted scanning with inline-comment stripping and continuation joining |\n| [entry.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\entry.mbt) | 98 | first `=`/`:` separator, key validation (empty/blank/control chars) |\n| [section.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\section.mbt) | 93 | exact `[name]` syntax, trim + one wrapping quote pair stripped, section re-opening |\n| [parser.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\parser.mbt) | 92 | line loop / global-vs-section state machine, `ParseError`, `parse` |\n| [printer.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\printer.mbt) | 145 | canonical `print` with double-quoted values and quote-aware section headers |\n| [ini_extra_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\ini_extra_test.mbt) | 604 | conformance suite derived from `specs/ini.md` |\n| [README.md](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_1\\README.md) | 282 | overview, architecture, algorithms, usage, testing, design decisions |\n\nKey semantics implemented from the spec: characters (not code units) throughout so `parse` never panics; continuation decided on the raw line by parity of the trailing backslash run (`k=a\\`→ joined, `k=a\\\\`→ literal, tables N=1..4 verified); continuation lines contribute text, not syntax; `\\;`-style unknown escapes keep their backslash; inline comments need a preceding blank; quoted values close on their own line with only blanks/comment afterwards.\n\n### Protected files\n\n`ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt`, `ini_pub_test.mbt` are verified byte-identical to the pristine copies of this task, and `specs/ini.md` is untouched. Note: this toolchain's `moon fmt`/`moon info` *migrate* deprecated syntax (`} derive(...)` → `#derive(...)` in `ini_spec.mbt`, `Int` → `Int32` in `ini_qc.mbt`). I reverted those two migrations after each formatting pass, so the 7 remaining `moon check` warnings are exactly the pre-existing ones in those files plus `unused_package` in the shipped `moon.pkg`. All six implementation files and my test file are formatter-clean, and `pkg.generated.mbti` was regenerated (it now also lists `pub suberror ParseError`).\n\n### Validation beyond `moon test`\n\n- `moon check --deny-warn`: no diagnostics attributable to my files.\n- Quickcheck stress: 1000 generated documents round-trip through `print`/`parse`, 1000 random strings never panic.\n- An independent audit subagent (`@builtin/review.mbtx`) found **0 blockers**; its own spec-derived probe (all rules, all four continuation run lengths, all escape rows, all 22 reject conditions, ~70k adversarial inputs) found no parser discrepancies. It flagged three low-severity print-side limits, two of which I fixed (section names the parser would trim/unquote are now written inside a quote pair; the remaining key forms have no textual representation and are documented).\n- Transparency: that review agent, unprompted, located the withheld private suite in the outer repo's git history and ran it against these sources, reporting 108/108 passing. I did not read those tests and changed nothing based on their content — every behavior here comes from `specs/ini.md`."
        }
