          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "Implemented a real INI parser and printer for this repo's dialect in MoonBit, at the module root so `@ini.parse` / `@ini.print` are the root package's own API.\n\n## What was built\n\n**Public API** (`declare`d in the untouched [ini_spec.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_spec.mbt)) is implemented by:\n- [parser.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\parser.mbt) — `parse`: line classification, document assembly (global + sections, reopen/last-wins)\n- [printer.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\printer.mbt) — `print`: always double-quoted values with `\\\\ \\\" \\n \\r \\t` escaping, header rendering\n\n**Supporting modules**\n- [errors.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\errors.mbt) — `pub suberror IniError(String)`, the single reject path (messages name the 1-based line)\n- [text.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\text.mbt) — blank/character helpers, trailing-backslash-run counting, control-code test\n- [lines.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\lines.mbt) — LF/CRLF physical line splitting into a `Line` record (view + line number)\n- [sections.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\sections.mbt) — header/name parsing: trimmed names, one wrapping quote pair stripped, quotes otherwise literal, empty/nested/unclosed rejected\n- [values.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\values.mbt) — quoted vs unquoted scanning, the three per-carrier escape sets (`\\\\ \\n \\r \\t` / +`\\\"` / only `\\\\ \\'`), inline comments (blank-before-marker), odd/even trailing-backslash continuations joined directly and decided on the raw line\n\nKey algorithms are the run-length continuation rule (`C:\\Program Files\\` continues, `...\\\\` ends with a literal backslash) and per-carrier escape decoding that copies untouched text as whole `StringView` slices so Unicode/surrogate pairs are never split.\n\n## Verification\n- `moon check`: **0 errors**; the only 7 warnings come from the vendored `ini_spec.mbt` / `ini_qc.mbt` / `ini_pub_test.mbt` (deprecated `derive(...)`, implicit trait-method promotion) and `moon.pkg`'s `core/test` import — files this task forbids editing. All package-owned files are warning-free and `moon fmt --check` clean.\n- `moon test`: **53/53 pass** — the 12 public tests plus 41 new tests in [ini_edge_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_edge_test.mbt) derived rule-by-rule from `specs/ini.md` (both separators/first-wins, trimming, key validation, comment rules, all escape tables, the N=1..4 continuation table, continuation-lines-are-data, CRLF, invalid forms, print round trips for awkward values and section names, and a deterministic fuzz pass proving `parse` never panics).\n- `moon info` regenerated [pkg.generated.mbti](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\pkg.generated.mbti). `moon fmt` also rewrites the vendored spec files (deprecated-syntax migration), so those three files were restored to their delivered content afterwards.\n- An independent audit found one real bug — section names containing both quote characters did not round-trip — which is fixed by always adding exactly one extra quote pair (the parser strips exactly one), with explicit round-trip tests added.\n\n## Documented judgment calls\n`README.md` (written from the actual code) records the dialect table, architecture, algorithms, and the ambiguity decisions: a trailing line break terminates the last line (so a marker at end of input is an error either way), continuation lines are appended verbatim as data, inline comments require a preceding blank, and section headers tolerate a trailing comment after `]` (symmetric with quoted values) while rejecting any other trailing text.\n"
